---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout>
  <article class="legal-page">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p><strong>Effective date:</strong> September 13, 2026</p>

    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how Eddies Games (“we”, “us”, or “our”)
      collects, uses, and shares information when you visit eddiesgames.xyz
      or play its browser games.
    </p>

    <h2>Information you provide</h2>

    <p>
      You do not need an account to play our games. Some games allow you to
      submit information to a leaderboard, which may include a display name,
      score, completion time, move count, difficulty, or other game results.
    </p>

    <p>
      Please do not use your full legal name or include personal information
      in a leaderboard display name. Leaderboard entries may be publicly
      visible and may be removed if they are inappropriate, fraudulent, or
      abusive.
    </p>

    <p>
      If you contact us by email, we receive your email address and the
      information you include in your message.
    </p>

    <h2>Information collected automatically</h2>

    <p>
      When you use the site, we and our service providers may automatically
      receive limited technical information, including:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>IP address</li>
      <li>Browser and device type</li>
      <li>Operating system</li>
      <li>Pages or games requested</li>
      <li>Approximate location derived from an IP address</li>
      <li>Performance, diagnostic, security, and error information</li>
      <li>Date and time of requests</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      This information may be processed through standard server logs,
      security services, hosting infrastructure, and advertising services.
    </p>

    <h2>Local storage and cookies</h2>

    <p>
      Some games may use browser storage to remember game progress,
      preferences, daily-game status, or local high scores. The site and its
      service providers may also use cookies or similar technologies for
      security, consent management, advertising, and measurement.
    </p>

    <p>
      See our <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a> for more information.
    </p>

    <h2>Advertising</h2>

    <p>
      We use Google AdSense to display and measure advertising. Third-party
      vendors, including Google, may use cookies to serve ads based on a
      visitor’s previous visits to this website or other websites.
    </p>

    <p>
      Google’s use of advertising cookies enables Google and its partners to
      serve personalized or non-personalized ads. Depending on your location,
      you may be asked to consent to advertising cookies and the processing of
      personal data before personalized advertising is shown.
    </p>

    <p>
      You can manage personalized advertising through
      <a
        href="https://adssettings.google.com/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        Google Ads Settings
      </a>.
      You may also be able to opt out of some third-party vendors’ uses of
      cookies for personalized advertising through
      <a
        href="https://optout.aboutads.info/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        YourAdChoices
      </a>.
    </p>

    <p>
      Information about how Google uses data from sites that use its services
      is available in
      <a
        href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        Google’s partner-sites policy
      </a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Consent and privacy choices</h2>

    <p>
      Visitors in applicable regions are shown a consent message provided
      through Google’s certified Consent Management Platform. The message
      allows visitors to consent, decline consent, or manage individual
      options.
    </p>

    <p>
      You can also control or delete cookies and site data using your browser
      settings. Removing site data may reset saved game progress,
      preferences, or consent choices.
    </p>

    <h2>How we use information</h2>

    <p>We may use information to:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>Provide and maintain the website and games</li>
      <li>Operate leaderboards and record submitted game results</li>
      <li>Remember game progress and preferences</li>
      <li>Detect cheating, spam, fraud, and technical abuse</li>
      <li>Diagnose errors and improve reliability</li>
      <li>Respond to questions and bug reports</li>
      <li>Display and measure advertising</li>
      <li>Comply with legal obligations</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Service providers</h2>

    <p>
      We use service providers to operate the site. These currently include
      Cloudflare for hosting, networking, security, and database
      infrastructure, and Google for advertising and consent management.
      These providers may process information according to their own privacy
      policies.
    </p>

    <h2>Data retention</h2>

    <p>
      We retain information only for as long as reasonably necessary to
      operate the site, maintain leaderboards, prevent abuse, resolve
      technical issues, and meet legal obligations.
    </p>

    <p>
      Public leaderboard entries may remain until they are removed, replaced,
      or the relevant leaderboard is reset. Local game data remains in your
      browser until the game removes it or you clear your browser’s site data.
    </p>

    <h2>Children’s privacy</h2>

    <p>
      Eddies Games is intended for a general audience. We do not knowingly
      collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a
      child has submitted personal information, contact us so that we can
      review and remove it where appropriate.
    </p>

    <h2>International visitors</h2>

    <p>
      Information may be processed in the United States or other countries
      where our service providers operate. Data-protection laws in those
      locations may differ from those in your country.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>

    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have rights concerning your
      personal information, including rights to request access, correction,
      or deletion. To make a request, contact us using the address below.
      We may need enough information to verify and process your request.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>

    <p>
      We may update this policy as the site, games, or services change. The
      revised effective date will be shown at the top of this page.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>

    <p>
      Email:
      <a href="mailto:eddie@eddiesgames.xyz">
        eddie@eddiesgames.xyz
      </a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .legal-page h1 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .legal-page h2 {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .legal-page p,
  .legal-page li {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .legal-page a {
    color: var(--ember);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .legal-page ul {
    padding-left: 1.4rem;
  }
</style>
